## Summary

Fixes duplicate `reused` progress reporting from `pnpm dedupe`.

During dedupe, resolution probes the store and can observe a provisional cache hit before materialization reports the package's authoritative terminal status. Both events were forwarded to the append-only progress counters, so a package already in the store could be counted twice. In the minimal reproduction from pnpm/pnpm#15303, 69 resolved packages were reported as 138 reused packages.

This change:

- records resolve-time store hits as provisional dedupe progress;
- shares install-scoped package-status claims with fetch and materialization;
- flushes only unclaimed provisional hits before terminal progress events;
- preserves fallback reporting for filtered and resolve-only dedupe runs;
- suppresses provisional reuse when an optional fetch fails;
- leaves ordinary install progress behavior unchanged through dedupe-specific progress keys.

> **Rebased onto pnpm/pnpm#15309** (agent maintainer update). That PR landed a narrower fix for pnpm/pnpm#15303: it skips the resolve-time `found_in_store` report unless the run is `--lockfile-only` or `--check`. Tested against current `main`, that approach leaves two cases with no reused packages reported at all:
>
> - `pnpm dedupe --filter <project>`;
> - a dedupe that resolves only because config disables materialization (for example `enableModulesDir: false`).
>
